<!-- SECTION 3 — EAVESDROPPER DETECTION -->
<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="s3" class="section">
<div class="section-num">Section 03</div>
<h2>Eavesdropper Detection</h2>

<p>What happens if Eve intercepts the quantum channel? Let's trace exactly what occurs.</p>

<div class="def">
  <div class="def-title">Eve's Dilemma</div>
  Eve sits between Alice and Bob: A → E → B. She must measure each qubit to learn information, then forward something to Bob. But she doesn't know which basis Alice used — she must guess.
</div>

<h3>Why Eve Gets Caught</h3>

<p>Eve guesses the wrong basis 50% of the time. When she measures in the wrong basis:</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="mstep"><div class="mstep-label">Example:</div><div class="mstep-body">Alice sends |0⟩ (Z-basis, bit 0). Eve measures in X-basis → gets |+⟩ or |−⟩ randomly, say |+⟩. Eve forwards |+⟩ to Bob.</div></div>
  <div class="mstep"><div class="mstep-label">Bob measures</div><div class="mstep-body">in Z-basis (matching Alice): P(Bob gets 1) = |⟨1|+⟩|² = 1/2 → <span class="c-n" style="font-weight:700;">error!</span> Bob should have gotten 0.</div></div>
  <div class="mstep"><div class="mstep-label">Net effect:</div><div class="mstep-body">When Alice and Bob use the same basis, there's a 25% chance of an error (50% Eve uses wrong basis × 50% Bob then gets wrong bit). This error is detectable in the security check!</div></div>
</div>

<div class="insight">
  <strong>The probability of Eve NOT being detected</strong> on N<sub>p</sub> published bits, given that she is eavesdropping, is:<br>
  <div class="math-block" style="margin-top:0.4rem;">
    <div class="eq">P(no detection) = P(no errors on Nₚ bits) = (1/2)<sup>Nₚ</sup></div>
    <div class="eq-note">&nbsp;&nbsp;→ as Nₚ increases, P(detection) = 1 − (1/2)<sup>Nₚ</sup> → 1</div>
  </div>
  Even with 20 published bits, P(detection) > 99.9999%!
</div>

<h3>Worked Example with Eve</h3>

<div class="math-block">
  <table class="bb84-table" style="font-size:0.73rem;">
    <tr>
      <th>Position</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th><th>5</th>
    </tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Alice bit</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Alice basis</td><td>⊕</td><td>⊗</td><td>⊕</td><td>⊗</td><td>⊕</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Tx qubit</td><td>|0⟩</td><td>|−⟩</td><td>|0⟩</td><td>|+⟩</td><td>|1⟩</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Eve basis</td><td>⊕</td><td>⊕</td><td>⊗</td><td>⊗</td><td>⊗</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Eve reads</td>
      <td style="color:var(--green)">0</td>
      <td style="color:var(--red)">?</td>
      <td style="color:var(--red)">?</td>
      <td style="color:var(--green)">0</td>
      <td style="color:var(--red)">?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Eve forwards</td><td>|0⟩</td><td>|0⟩ or |1⟩</td><td>|+⟩ or |−⟩</td><td>|+⟩</td><td>|+⟩ or |−⟩</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Bob basis</td><td>⊕</td><td>⊗</td><td>⊕</td><td>⊗</td><td>⊕</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Bob reads</td>
      <td class="match">0 ✓</td>
      <td>? (rnd)</td>
      <td>? (rnd)</td>
      <td class="match">0 ✓</td>
      <td>? (rnd)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Bases match?</td>
      <td class="match">✓</td><td class="match">✓</td><td class="match">✓</td><td class="match">✓</td><td class="match">✓</td>
    </tr>
    <tr><td style="background:#f5f2ea;font-weight:600;">Error possible?</td>
      <td>No</td>
      <td style="color:var(--red);font-weight:700;">Yes 50%</td>
      <td style="color:var(--red);font-weight:700;">Yes 50%</td>
      <td>No</td>
      <td style="color:var(--red);font-weight:700;">Yes 50%</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <div style="margin-top:0.5rem;font-size:0.78rem;color:var(--muted);">Green = correct reading (Eve used same basis as Alice) · ? = random result (wrong basis)</div>
</div>

<p>In the security check (step 5), Alice and Bob compare some of their kept bits. If Eve was eavesdropping, errors appear. With enough published bits, Eve is virtually certain to be detected.</p>

